<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oleg Sviatoslavich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1053–1115</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Oleg Gorislavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oleg Sviatoslavich was a Rurikid prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-ii-of-kiev">Sviatoslav II of Kiev</a> and ancestor of the Olgovichi princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>. Driven into exile, he used Tmutarakan on the Taman peninsula as a base, at times with Cuman allies, and left it in 1094 to fight for Chernigov. His feuds with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-ii-monomakh">Vladimir Monomakh</a> earned him the name Gorislavich, 'son of sorrow', in the Tale of Igor's Campaign.</p></div>
